{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00396",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.53,
      "end_seconds": 4.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thank you for staying late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.68,
      "end_seconds": 13.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.17,
      "end_seconds": 17.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Hmm, thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.78,
      "end_seconds": 26.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "So, it's a pounding headache, mostly. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.56,
      "end_seconds": 29.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.21,
      "end_seconds": 38.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "For two months, I'd say. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.34,
      "end_seconds": 40.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.19,
      "end_seconds": 49.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "Well, um, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.0,
      "end_seconds": 55.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.42,
      "end_seconds": 59.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "It's, It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.98,
      "end_seconds": 62.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.12,
      "end_seconds": 68.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Nausea goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.04,
      "end_seconds": 76.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "So, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 76.25,
      "end_seconds": 81.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.56,
      "end_seconds": 83.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.78,
      "end_seconds": 95.45,
      "duration_seconds": 10.67,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.77,
      "end_seconds": 101.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Honestly, on and off. A five out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.48,
      "end_seconds": 108.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Any loss of consciousness or neck stiffness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.47,
      "end_seconds": 120.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.17,
      "text": "Oh, no, no loss of consciousness, no neck stiffness. I did have flashing lights before it starts at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.38,
      "end_seconds": 127.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any slurred speech or double vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.62,
      "end_seconds": 130.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Oh, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.35,
      "end_seconds": 135.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Alright, and weakness in the arms or legs, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.34,
      "end_seconds": 141.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "No weakness in the arms or legs, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.3,
      "end_seconds": 145.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.07,
      "end_seconds": 148.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.28,
      "end_seconds": 153.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.41,
      "end_seconds": 163.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.28,
      "text": "Um, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.43,
      "end_seconds": 166.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.78,
      "end_seconds": 172.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "I'm on sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed for my migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 172.77,
      "end_seconds": 180.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the sumatriptan was 25 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.7,
      "end_seconds": 183.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.23,
      "end_seconds": 204.1,
      "duration_seconds": 18.87,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so no, I left it at home. I mean, I take telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I'm on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.96,
      "end_seconds": 211.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.57,
      "end_seconds": 223.19,
      "duration_seconds": 11.62,
      "text": "Migraines, for two years. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.85,
      "end_seconds": 224.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.4,
      "end_seconds": 235.1,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "I've got high blood pressure. Oh, um, I've got anxiety. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.48,
      "end_seconds": 245.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "Alright. Yes, I can see the high blood pressure in your file as well. What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.03,
      "end_seconds": 249.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so my father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.31,
      "end_seconds": 254.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.7,
      "end_seconds": 268.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.05,
      "end_seconds": 297.17,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 84 beats a minute, BP is 110 over 73, respiratory rate 16, temp 36.7 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.86,
      "end_seconds": 302.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.71,
      "end_seconds": 306.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.58,
      "end_seconds": 325.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Power in all four limbs is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.19,
      "end_seconds": 330.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.85,
      "end_seconds": 346.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Neck is supple, no stiffness at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.8,
      "end_seconds": 371.75,
      "duration_seconds": 20.95,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with migraine with aura at this stage. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Tension-type headache is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.59,
      "end_seconds": 375.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Doctor, uh, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.22,
      "end_seconds": 394.58,
      "duration_seconds": 18.36,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's migraine with aura, and we'll know more once the an MRI of the brain is back. I'd like to arrange an MRI of the brain for recurrent headaches. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.11,
      "end_seconds": 427.25,
      "duration_seconds": 31.14,
      "text": "I'd like you to take domperidone, 10 milligrams, when nauseous, as needed. You take it by mouth. That's for migraine nausea. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. I'm prescribing propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day, for three months. That should help with migraine prevention. Try not to skip meals and keep your sleep regular. Keep a headache diary, things like skipped meals, poor sleep, certain foods and the weather."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.82,
      "end_seconds": 449.28,
      "duration_seconds": 20.46,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 449.73,
      "end_seconds": 452.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Okay, um, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 453.22,
      "end_seconds": 469.41,
      "duration_seconds": 16.19,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you have the worst headache of your life or any weakness. Please come and see me in six weeks. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 470.06,
      "end_seconds": 475.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Oh, you know, no, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}